WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:01.820
Who doesn't love a twist ending?

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:05.940
There's just something about having your expectations
set up and then smashed to smithereens that

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:09.040
makes every movie-goer fall in love with cinema
all over again.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:13.240
Luckily, plenty of movies boast enough twists
and turns to make our heads spin — and these

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.660
are just a handful of the films that have
done it best.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:21.320
For those out of the loop, Fight Club follows
Ed Norton's unnamed protagonist, an insomniac

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:24.100
working a job he hates to buy things he doesn't
need.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:26.820
"With insomnia, nothing's real.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:29.820
Everything's far away.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.820
Everything's a copy of a copy."

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:36.400
After his apartment is blown to pieces in
an explosion, he moves into a rundown house

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:41.340
with Brad Pitt's Tyler Durden, his opposite
in every way ⁠— cool, focused, and ready

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:42.460
to tear the world down.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:47.060
But what begins as an unlikely friendship
gradually escalates into a bitter rivalry

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:49.740
and, eventually, a pretty heated butting of
heads.

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:53.720
To make a long story short, the two start
a fight club to help men express themselves

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:58.320
and relieve their stress… but it quickly
morphs into a full-blown anti-capitalist terrorist

00:00:58.320 --> 00:00:58.820
cell.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:02.900
By the time Norton's character realizes that
he and Durden are the same person, it's too

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:05.240
late to stop the plan they've put in place.

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:09.460
The movie ends with the destruction of the
city's financial district, wiping out everyone's

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:09.960
debt.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:16.080
In case you slept through 2017, here's the
gist of Jordan Peele's super-popular, ultra-profitable

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:20.900
Get Out: When Chris, a young black man, meets
the parents of his white girlfriend Rose for

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:25.040
the first time, we soon come to realize that
something isn't quite right with her family.

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:28.460
After Chris meets a peculiar black guest at
the family's garden party …

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:29.940
"GET OUT!"

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:30.600
"Yo."

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:31.610
"GET OUT!"

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:32.980
"Yo, chill, man!"

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:37.119
… viewers are led to believe that the protagonist
is about to be brainwashed into some kind

00:01:37.119 --> 00:01:42.070
of modern-day slavery, but the final reveal
is even more mind-blowing: It turns out Chris

00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:46.680
is in the clutches of the Order of Coagula,
a cult that transplants the brains of old,

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:49.540
rich white people into the bodies of young
black people.

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:53.280
"I want… your eye, man.

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:57.480
I want those things you see through."

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:02.140
Unlike those that came before him, Chris manages
to escape this awful fate, stuffing his ears

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:04.100
with cotton to avoid being hypnotized.

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:08.300
He fights his way outside and is ultimately
rescued by his best friend Rod.

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:12.760
This wasn't the original ending, however — Peele
also shot a version in which the cops show

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:16.980
up instead of Rod and an innocent Chris is
jailed for killing his kidnappers.

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:22.760
South Korean director Park Chan-wook made
inroads in Hollywood in 2013 after helming

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:27.600
two English-language films, the psychological
drama Stoker and the Chris Evans-led sci-fi

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:28.820
thriller Snowpiercer.

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:33.220
While both drew praise from critics — with
the latter boasting an impressive 95 percent

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:37.170
Certified Fresh rating on Rotten Tomatoes
— most reviewers agreed that Park's best

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:41.880
work was done domestically, and the jewel
in his Korean filmography is undoubtedly Oldboy.

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:46.800
The film follows a drunk named Oh Dae-su who's
framed for the murder of his wife and imprisoned

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:49.580
in an iron-doored hotel room by an unknown
man.

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:53.900
When he's randomly released 15 years later,
he aims to track down his captor with the

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:57.100
help of a young female sushi chef who takes
him in after his ordeal.

00:02:57.550 --> 00:03:01.900
The woman and Oh Dae-su fall for each other
and begin a sexual relationship, though unbeknownst

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:04.560
to the pair this is all part of the captor's
grand plan.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:08.600
Oh Dae-su and the young woman are actually
father and daughter, which Oh's tormentor

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:10.500
takes great pleasure in revealing.

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:16.000
The final installment of a trilogy M. Night
Shyamalan began with 2000's Unbreakable, Glass

00:03:16.001 --> 00:03:20.830
reunites Bruce Willis and Samuel L. Jackson's
characters, David Dunn — a.k.a the Overseer

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:23.720
— and Elijah Price, better known as "Mr.
Glass."

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:28.900
Both are banged up in a psychiatric ward alongside
James McAvoy's Kevin Wendell Crumb — a.k.a

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:34.680
the Horde from 2016's Split — a man suffering
from an extreme case of dissociative identity

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:35.180
disorder.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:39.820
All three are under the care of Dr. Ellie
Staple, a psychiatrist who specializes in

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:43.040
patients who have become convinced that they
have superhuman abilities.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:47.360
Staple spends the majority of the film attempting
to convince the men that they're delusional,

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:48.540
and she's pretty convincing.

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:51.240
At times, against our better judgment, we
believe her.

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:55.900
"You've convinced yourselves you have extraordinary
gifts, like something out of a comic book.

00:03:56.120 --> 00:04:00.160
I am here to discuss the possibility that
you are mistaken."

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:01.400
Of course, she's wrong.

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:05.800
It transpires that Staple is part of a secret
society that has been actively repressing

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:07.540
super-powered people for years.

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:11.280
Price is killed by the Beast, and Staple's
men murder Dunn and Crumb.

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:15.600
There's one final twist, however — Price
hacked the institution's security cameras.

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:19.520
Footage of Dunn and Crumb's super-powered
showdown is leaked to the public, revealing

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:22.140
the existence of superhumans to the world.

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:27.140
A film containing one of the creepiest shock
twists in recent years, Orphan follows a couple

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:31.409
played by Vera Farmiga and Peter Sarsgaard
as they try to move on with their lives after

00:04:31.409 --> 00:04:32.900
the death of their unborn child.

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:37.120
In an attempt to save their marriage, the
pair decide to go ahead with their plans for

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:41.000
a third child, adopting a quiet 9-year-old
Russian girl named Esther.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:43.500
At least, they're lead to believe she's nine.

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:46.220
"I don't think mommy likes me very much."

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:49.400
"Hey, that's not true — mommy loves you."

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:53.280
"It’s alright, it must be hard to love an
adopted child as much as your own."

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:58.300
In truth, Esther is a 33-year-old woman named
Leena Klammer, a psychopath with a growth

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:02.860
disorder who's spent the majority of her life
posing as a pigtailed child and being repeatedly

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:03.360
adopted.

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:05.380
Why does she need to keep finding new families?

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:07.820
She keeps trying to get it on with the dads.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:12.780
We watch in sheer horror as Esther sets about
seducing her new father and proceeds to kill

00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:14.060
him when he isn't receptive.

